# These are Forge's files, imported byte-identically, and the point of that is
# that anyone can re-verify them against upstream with `cmp`. The repo root's
# `* text=auto eol=lf` would silently rewrite the two CRLF recipes
# (`Pioneer Cube.draft`, `The Arena Cube.draft`) to LF on commit, so a
# round-trip through git would no longer match `forge-gui/res/draft/`.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion here without marking the files
# binary, so they still diff as text.
#
# Nothing reads these bytes literally — `parseDraftRecipe` splits on /\r?\n/ and
# trims, and there is a test asserting the two CRLF files parse identically to
# the LF ones. This is purely about keeping the import verifiable.
*.draft -text
